Consider the tensor product

\begin{align}
\F_1(u_1)\otimes\F_1(u_2)\otimes\F_1(u_3)\otimes\F_2(u_4)\otimes\F_2(u_5)\otimes \F_3(u_6)\,, \qquad C=s_1^3s_2^2s_3.
\end{align}

The
matrix $B$ is given by

\begin{align}
&B=
\begin{pmatrix}
-t_2t_3(s_1+s_1^{-1}) & t_2t_3  &     0     &        0      &    0  \\
t_2t_3 &-t_2t_3(s_1+s_1^{-1})& t_2t_3   & 0  &    0           \\
0     &t_2t_3                &t_3^2  & t_1t_3       &      0         \\
0   &            0          &t_3t_t  &-t_1t_3 (s_2+s_2^{-1})& t_1t_3    \\
0   &      0&0& t_1t_3 &t_1^2
\end{pmatrix}.
\end{align}

We picture this matrix as a Dynkin diagram where
a circle represents a bosonic node and a crossed circle
a fermionic node. We also attach a marking by $1,2,3$ to each vertex, indicating its type.

\begin{align*}
\begin{tikzpicture}
\dynkin[root radius=.1cm, edge length=1.3cm, labels={1,1,3,2,1}]{A}{ootot}
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{align*}

\qed
